  "details": "VRC Animator Tracking Control does not save its state and reverts on unity restart - it seems that only the initial changes are saved when you first add the script.\n\n100% repro on multiple users (humans & accounts), different machines, etc.. with latest sdk/unity (as of 2024-03-01, reproduced this several months apart, first encountered in November 2023...)\n\nSteps:\n\n1) Have an avatar with some kind of gesture or fx controller.\n\n2) Add a tracking control script to some layers and change some values to tracking/animation - hands or face tracking is a good test.\n\n3) Upload your avatar, see that it behaves as expected.\n\n4) Restart Unity\n\n5) Change some of the tracking/animation values. (Optionally hit CTRL+S...)\n\n6) Upload your avatar and observe that it behaves as expected with your new changes.\n\n7) Restart Unity\n\n8) Observe that the tracking/animation values have reverted to your original values and the latest changes are not present. Any now uploaded avatar will also be (obviously) reverted.",
